INKYTUNE PRIVACY POLICY

Effective date: October 5, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how InkyTune and its Doodle Synth, Doodle FX, and Doodle MIDI Audio Unit extensions handle information on iPhone and iPad.

1. OVERVIEW

InkyTune does not require an InkyTune account. Music generation, playback, and audio processing take place on your device. The App does not include advertising, third-party analytics, cross-app tracking, or online generative AI.

When iCloud is available for InkyTune, saved music projects sync through your Apple Account. Apple provides the iCloud service. The developer does not operate a server that receives or stores your projects.

2. INFORMATION STORED BY THE APP

InkyTune stores music projects on your device. A project may contain its name, drawn melody, notes, arrangement, style, tempo, key, scale, generation settings, track settings, and modification date. The App also stores interface preferences, AUv3 Shared Library presets you choose to save, and temporary audio or MIDI files created during export.

This information is used to save and restore your work, generate and play music, export files, and support the included Audio Unit extensions.

3. ICLOUD PROJECT SYNC

If iCloud Drive is available to InkyTune, the App automatically stores copies of saved projects in its app-specific iCloud container and syncs them across devices signed in to the same Apple Account. Project changes and deletions sync when the devices are online. If iCloud is unavailable, your projects remain available locally on the device.

This feature does not automatically sync exported audio or MIDI files, interface preferences, or AUv3 Shared Library presets. Apple handles iCloud storage and transfer under its own terms and privacy policy. The developer does not access your synced project content through a developer-operated service.

You can stop future syncing by disabling iCloud access for InkyTune or iCloud Drive in your device settings, where available. Existing iCloud data can be managed through your Apple Account’s iCloud storage settings.

4. AUDIO UNIT EXTENSIONS

Doodle Synth, Doodle FX, and Doodle MIDI can run inside compatible third-party Audio Unit host apps. Audio, MIDI events, and automation handled by these extensions remain in the local Audio Unit hosting environment. The extensions do not send this content to the developer.

Songs and presets that you add to the AUv3 Shared Library are stored in an Apple App Group container shared by InkyTune and its included extensions on your device. This library is separate from iCloud project sync.

A third-party host app may handle information under its own privacy policy.

5. EXPORTING AND SHARING

InkyTune creates audio and MIDI exports locally. If you choose to share or save a file using Apple’s share sheet, Files, AirDrop, iCloud Drive, or another app or service, that destination may receive and process the file under its own privacy policy. InkyTune does not automatically upload exported files.

6. DATA COLLECTION

The developer does not collect your project content, contact details, location, contacts, photos, camera data, microphone recordings, payment card details, advertising identifiers, browsing history, or in-app behavioral analytics through the App. InkyTune does not sell data or share it for advertising or tracking.

Apple independently handles App Store purchases, downloads, iCloud storage, and other Apple services. Depending on your settings or TestFlight participation, Apple may provide the developer with aggregated App Store metrics or crash and diagnostic reports. InkyTune does not add its own analytics or diagnostic collection service.

7. RETENTION AND DELETION

Local projects and preferences remain on your device until you delete or change them, or uninstall the App. When iCloud sync is available, saved projects may also remain in your iCloud storage.

Deleting a project in InkyTune removes it from the project library and propagates that change to synced devices when they connect. If simultaneous edits conflict, the App may preserve a separate conflict copy so neither version is silently lost. You can delete a conflict copy like any other project.

Uninstalling the App may not remove copies already stored in iCloud. You can delete projects in the App while iCloud sync is available or manage the App’s data in your Apple Account’s iCloud storage settings. Files you previously exported to another destination must be deleted there separately. Apple’s retention and recovery of iCloud data are governed by Apple’s policies.

The developer does not maintain an InkyTune account or a server-side project record to access, correct, export, or delete.

8. SECURITY

InkyTune relies on Apple’s application sandbox, App Group access controls, and operating-system protections for local data. Apple handles iCloud storage and transfer. We recommend protecting your device and Apple Account and keeping your operating system up to date.

9. CHILDREN’S PRIVACY

InkyTune does not knowingly collect personal information from children or other users through a developer-operated service. The App is not designed to request personal information.

10. INTERNATIONAL DATA TRANSFERS

The developer does not operate a server that receives App data. Apple may process iCloud and App Store data under its own terms and privacy policy. Transfers you initiate through third-party services are handled by the selected service.

11. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY

We may update this Privacy Policy when the App’s features or data practices change. The revised policy will show a new effective date. We will update the relevant App Store privacy disclosures when required.

12. CONTACT

If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or InkyTune’s privacy practices, contact the developer through the Support URL on InkyTune’s App Store product page.
